{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "date": "2026-11-17",
  "scope": "Six registered chassis item displays, with source-only placement/recovery review. Static export and parsing only; no runtime/test/render execution.",
  "findings": {
    "gui": "The authored vehicle front is +Z. Existing GUI yaw225 presented the rear (also visible in the historical native preview). Miniature-only yaw45 presents the cab/glacis/main gun toward the GUI camera while retaining roof visibility, scale and centering.",
    "firstPerson": "ItemTransform.apply(leftHand) negates authored Y/Z angles. Previous right45/left225 became actual45/135; new right45/left45 becomes45/-45. Both hands now have corresponding front views. The eventual player arm transform still needs real-player verification.",
    "geometry": "All six already contain detailed production geometry (truck78/APC138/tank161). No generic generated-icon fallback, texture lookup failure or missing body part was found. Every element, UV, skin reference and other display transform is preserved byte-for-byte at the JSON value level.",
    "muzzle": "Current main_muzzle is a solid authored cuboid, but the available local reference records do not prove the original bore geometry, wall thickness or inner diameter. No guessed hollow-barrel geometry is introduced in this display correction."
  },
  "localEvidence": {
    "coordinateContract": "art/military-vehicles/README.md: author +Z is the vehicle front; positive Y is up. Model source and production entity renderer use the same convention.",
