        }
      },
      "semantics": "ItemTransform applies scale then rotationXYZ; left-hand negates Y/Z and translation X. GuiGraphics GUI scale(16,-16,16) preserves the depth sign."
    },
    "originalReferenceBoundary": "art/military-vehicles/reference-observations.json contains the existing P1/P2 visual observations. Its ignored source-image cache is not present in this workspace. Packaged model coordinates, seats, muzzle lengths, palette and UV pixels are authored Minecraft adaptations, not extracted Prototype meshes/materials."
  },
  "placementReview": {
    "entry": "VehicleRegistry.ChassisItem.useOn is reached by the actual right-click block path. PrototypeSurvivalLock preserves the chassis item use while declining block interaction, allows main-hand PASS to an offhand chassis, and client combat handlers decline attack-form capture when either hand holds a placement item.",
    "freshState": "The six registered items create their matching faction/chassis entity. MilitaryVehicle constructor starts at definition.maxHealth; VehicleInventory starts ammunition at zero. Successful placement assigns player UUID ownership. These are fresh vehicles, not recovered vehicle snapshots.",
    "validation": "settlePlacement checks loaded support, water, physical hull/body clearance; rejection discards the temporary entity, reports the reason and does not shrink the item. Item shrink happens only after addFreshEntity succeeds.",
    "recovery": "No whole-vehicle packing/recovery item path or chassis ItemStack state codec exists. Shift-empty-hand is the existing hijack path; it does not pack health/ammunition/ownership into a chassis item. A damaged-vehicle recovery/replacement round trip therefore is not an implemented feature and is not claimed as verified.",
    "sourceBoundary": "No unsupported Prototype whole-vehicle packing mechanic was added. Existing supply, repair, persistence, ownership and destruction paths remain unchanged.",
    "existingDeferredCoverage": "VehiclePlacementInteractionGameTest includes six variants, real right-click entry, combat forms, offhand, ordinary supported ground and rejection/no-consumption cases. They were not rerun in this task."
  },
